From 6f61b953086c1bdc908fecb9861086979b6e8694 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gezim <gezimos@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 20:28:34 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Kompakt: the volume dialog shows one slider

shouldBeVisibleH() added the default (media) row beside the active one
whenever the active stream was the voice call, ring, alarm, accessibility or
a remote stream. In a call that put a media slider next to the call slider,
and our outline (0067) wraps every visible row while the white column only
backs the last one, so the second slider sat in a see-through gap. The media
row no longer joins another row: the dialog shows the slider the keys
change, inside one white, outlined column.

Change-Id: I2534af05a4c25805cb37dbb8858a43e5a2829aab
---
 .../src/com/android/systemui/volume/VolumeDialogImpl.java  | 7 ++-----
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/packages/SystemUI/src/com/android/systemui/volume/VolumeDialogImpl.java b/packages/SystemUI/src/com/android/systemui/volume/VolumeDialogImpl.java
index 76eea0ee6645..bd926ea447a5 100644
--- a/packages/SystemUI/src/com/android/systemui/volume/VolumeDialogImpl.java
+++ b/packages/SystemUI/src/com/android/systemui/volume/VolumeDialogImpl.java
@@ -1694,12 +1694,9 @@ public class VolumeDialogImpl implements VolumeDialog, Dumpable,
                 return true;
             }
 
+            // Kompakt: media never joins another slider; the white column backs one slider only.
             if (row.defaultStream) {
-                return activeRow.stream == STREAM_RING
-                        || activeRow.stream == STREAM_ALARM
-                        || activeRow.stream == STREAM_VOICE_CALL
-                        || activeRow.stream == STREAM_ACCESSIBILITY
-                        || mDynamic.get(activeRow.stream);
+                return false;
             }
 
             // Continue to display row if it is visible to user.
